            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to stop, then the Russian for to come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: постепенно",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "постепенно (postépenno) — \"gradually, little by little\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Постепенно все поняли правила игры. Postépenno vse pónyali právila igrý. Gradually everyone understood the rules of the game."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The adverb of постепенный (postépennyy) \"gradual\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "постепенно (postépenno) is built on по and степень \"a degree, a step\", inherited from Proto-Slavic stepenĭ (EtymDB): step by step."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
